WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.335 --> 00:00:01.076
Jesus said,

2
00:00:01.076 --> 00:00:06.327
"call no man your father upon earth." So why do Catholics call priests Father?

3
00:00:06.777 --> 00:00:08.796
First, read the whole passage.

4
00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:13.576
In the same breath he says call no one teacher, and call no one master.

5
00:00:13.576 --> 00:00:17.346
Yet almost every Christian has called someone a teacher.

6
00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:22.665
Jesus is using a strong image against the pride of the leaders in front of him,

7
00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:23.944
not banning a word.

8
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:27.087
Second, look at how the apostles talked.

9
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:31.799
Saint Paul writes to the Corinthians, "in Christ Jesus, by the gospel,

10
00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:35.300
I have begotten you." He calls himself their father.

11
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.541
Saint Stephen, full of the Holy Spirit, opens his speech, "Men,

12
00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:44.254
brethren and fathers." Saint John writes, "I write unto you, fathers."

13
00:00:44.704 --> 00:00:49.012
If those words broke the rule, the apostles broke it constantly.

14
00:00:49.462 --> 00:00:54.646
What Jesus forbids is giving anyone the place that belongs to God the Father.

15
00:00:54.646 --> 00:00:58.080
A priest is called father for the reason Paul gave:

16
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.503
he's meant to care for you like one.
